 11	//! (its shared build and its own solve), then, for an attempt used as a
 12	//! verification, its verification pass (shared data and pass), then the
 13	//! decision on the attempt before it (the stop rule, charged to that
 14	//! candidate). The next segment stops at its first budget check
 15	//! (`StageGuard::test`) with `Unresolved(Budget(Case))`. So a prefix's heap
 16	//! peak is the high-water mark through segment j, plus the allocations the
 17	//! next segment makes before that check (derived in RETURN).
